config BR2_PACKAGE_RNSBOX_PYTHON_BLUEZERO
	bool "rnsbox-python-bluezero"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_DBUS_PYTHON # runtime (module-level `import dbus`)
	help
	  A Python library for Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE) peripheral mode
	  on Linux: registers GATT applications and LE advertisements
	  with BlueZ over D-Bus. Used by ble-reticulum's GATT server
	  (BLE peripheral mode - other Reticulum nodes and phone clients
	  connect INBOUND over it).

	  This is buildroot's python-bluezero 0.9.1 (same sdist, same
	  version) packaged under a separate symbol on purpose: the
	  in-tree python-bluezero pulls python-gobject, whose
	  gobject-introspection dependency needs a glibc toolchain - the
	  RNSBox Raspberry Pi image is musl. bluezero itself is
	  pure Python and only needs dbus-python (dbus.mainloop.glib
	  comes from dbus-python, not PyGObject).

	  https://ukBaz.github.io/bluezero/
